 is uh  the best possible path forward right is  uh is one where the world continues to  improve  uh and technology plays a big part of it  so uh not only do i agree but i'm uh i'm  hoping that that is the case as well  um yeah well we can do our part as  investors  to help support those companies  absolutely i always ask the same two  questions to uh to wrap up and then you  get to ask me one to uh to end it but  the first one is just what is the most  important book that you have ever read  wow oh my gosh there's so many  um it's hard to narrow it down but  i i talk about this book all the time  um it's jane eyre by charlotte bronte  i i guess this is probably  unconventional to mention on your  podcast but it's a  romance novel um why do you like that  one  i read it when i was 13 years old and  just  immediately felt like  it felt like my eyes were open to  a brand new color that had previously  not been visible to me  yeah it just describes love  and emotions in such a beautiful  way like the passages between jane and  rochester  in that novel are i think some of the  most beautiful  sentences that have ever been written in  the english language  and i yeah i just have a  keen appreciation for beauty um  and i appreciate  love i think it's why we're put on this  earth i think  we exist for love um and i think that  novel  encapsulates a lot of that yeah and how  much of it do you think was just  uh the period in time when you read it  right kind of at 13 years old  um if you'd read it at a different you  know point your life do you think it  would have had the same impact  or maybe it hadn't had more more or less  impact  like if i had read it as a jaded adult  um i think it helps me from from  i i think it reading it when i did has  helped me  resist becoming jaded as an adult  that's a great answer uh second question  is uh much more fun  which is aliens are you a believer or  non-believer absolutely  oh yes absolutely without hesitation i  mean just mathemat